                            <comment id="17391699" author="stevel@apache.org" created="Mon, 2 Aug 2021 16:59:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;just looking at this. Any specific reason not to have overwrite the default?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;it saves the overhead of an HTTP head probe against any of the object stores, and for any job where the  output committer has created a unique dir for that task attempt, no risk of conflict unless somehow the task really has decided to create two files with the same name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Has anyone ever encountered conflicts?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
